{%- comment -%}
  A price as the money filters print it in the shopper's currency. When Theme settings → Currency
  format → Round prices to whole amounts is on, prices show the way froyaorganics.com shows them:
  whole amounts on the product pages ($32.40 shows as $32, $23.33 as $23), exact amounts from the
  cart on. The cart drawer, the cart page and the checkout button pass exact: true, which keeps the
  cents and only drops a whole amount's ".00" ($72, $64.80), so the cart always reads like checkout.
  Only what the storefront prints changes. The cart, Kaching and checkout keep the exact prices,
  and the theme's own comparisons (whether a saving shows, the shipping goal) still use the cents.

  amount   the price in cents
  format   'with_currency' prints it like money_with_currency (code after it), 'without_trailing_zeros'
           like money_without_trailing_zeros, anything else like money
  exact    true keeps the exact price while rounding is on (the cart); a whole amount loses its ".00".
           No effect while rounding is off.
  Prints the price and nothing else; capture it to use it in a sentence or an attribute:
    capture saving_money
      render 'money', amount: saving
    endcapture
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if settings.round_prices and amount != nil
    if exact
      assign value = amount
    else
      assign value = amount | divided_by: 100.0 | round | times: 100
    endif
    assign short = value | money_without_trailing_zeros
    if format == 'with_currency'
      assign coded = value | money_with_currency
      assign padded = value | money
      if padded != short
        comment
          A whole amount. No filter prints the currency code without the decimals, so the number
          itself (35.00) loses its zero decimals inside the coded price ($35.00 USD), whatever
          symbol or markup the format puts around it. An amount with cents ($64.80) prints the
          same either way and is left alone.
        endcomment
        assign number = value | money_without_currency
        assign number_size = number.size | minus: 3
        assign trimmed = number | slice: 0, number_size
        assign coded = coded | replace: number, trimmed
      endif
      echo coded
    else
      echo short
    endif
  elsif format == 'with_currency'
    echo amount | money_with_currency
  elsif format == 'without_trailing_zeros'
    echo amount | money_without_trailing_zeros
  else
    echo amount | money
  endif
-%}
